WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:04.100
Horror is one of the genres most often maligned
by critics.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.550
On one hand, that's because a lot of horror
movies are pretty awful, and they earn their

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:08.360
bad reviews.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.420
But there are also plenty of great horror
films that happen to be critical failures.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.520
The average viewer might avoid some of these
movies for their low Rotten Tomatoes scores,

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.000
but that number can be deceiving.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.180
Here are just a few of horror cinema's critical
failures that are actually worth your time.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:23.520
Lords of Salem

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.000
While 2013's Lords of Salem might not reach
the levels of exploitation nirvana that director

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.750
Rob Zombie achieved in The Devil's Rejects,
it's perhaps his most interesting project,

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.880
the surreal tale of a woman who finds herself
in the snares of a centuries-in-the-making

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.140
plot initiated by a coven of witches.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.180
Critics slapped it with a low rating on Rotten
Tomatoes, complaining that it failed to deliver

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.899
the scares it seemed to promise.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.360
To be fair, that's not an incorrect observation.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.670
Relatively free of gore, the film is instead
something of an experimental tone piece, resulting

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.760
in a hypnotic, atmospheric film that's sure
to unsettle and intrigue viewers willing to

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.400
embrace abstract thrills.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.960
Dead Silence

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.830
Considering the fact that James Wan's filmography
contains classics like Saw, Insidious, and

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:18.580
The Conjuring, if Dead Silence is known as
his worst film, that's still not too much

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.200
of a knock.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.800
While far from perfect, it utilizes the classic
horror technique of taking things that are

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:27.610
already frightening in real life, in this
case, ventriloquists and their terrifying

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:31.560
puppets, and then making them the sources
of actual supernatural phenomena.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.600
Even a middling horror movie is going to be
pretty scary when the protagonist is facing

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.940
a ghost ventriloquist who cuts the tongues
out of her victims.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.500
"Your voice is mine now."

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.030
All things considered, it's admittedly not
anything special in terms of plot or writing,

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.340
which is likely why it didn't stick with the
critics who gave it such a low rating on Rotten

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.060
Tomatoes.

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:56.780
But boasting some great production design,
a perfectly solid cast, and a killer twist

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.560
ending, Dead Silence is still a fun little
entry in the filmography of a director who

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.020
has helped shape mainstream horror over the
last decade.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.300
All the Boys Love Mandy Lane

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.920
Occasionally a movie's poor Rotten Tomatoes
score is less indicative of a lack of quality

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.700
and more an indicator of a film's divisiveness.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.450
Among these films is All the Boys Love Mandy
Lane, which, according to The Washington Post,

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.620
was shot in 2006 and then delayed for seven
years.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.010
It's a polarizing effort that boasts a critical
reception split almost down the middle.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:30.770
Detractors felt it was nothing more than a
run-of-the-mill slasher movie, while fans

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:34.260
of the film praise its innovative visuals
and storytelling restraint.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.200
The story centers around a group of teens
who invite the super-popular Mandy Lane to

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:42.340
a secluded ranch for a weekend getaway, and
quickly find themselves being picked off one

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.960
by one by a deranged stalker.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:48.340
The movie seems to take no delight in its
kills, instead making the audience recognize

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.540
the gravity of each.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.960
Even if you find the movie to be a failure,
it's an interesting one for sure.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.300
Jennifer's Body

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.460
There's something to be said for a movie that
knows what it is, and the 2009 horror romp

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.769
Jennifer's Body knows exactly what it is:
the kind of film you'd watch with your friends

00:03:02.769 --> 00:03:03.400
late at night.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.220
It tells the story of a rock band's satanic
ritual gone wrong, leaving high school "It

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.220
Girl" Jennifer possessed by a demon that feeds
on the flesh of men.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.300
"Jennifer's evil.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.360
"I know."

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.200
"No, I'm mean she's actually evil.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.760
Not high school evil."

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.520
Featuring a stellar cast, the most quotable
horror movie script in decades, and a killer

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:27.960
soundtrack, it's some of the most fun you
can have watching a modern horror movie.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.819
"I am not insecure, needy, God, that's a joke.

00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:33.500
How could I ever be insecure?

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.480
I was the snowflake queen."

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:40.040
Unfortunately, critics weren't quite sure
what to make of it in 2009, and it's got a

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.840
bummer of a Rotten Tomatoes score.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:46.120
Jennifer's Body isn't quite old enough to
have built up a cult following or to have

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.320
received a critical reevaluation, but we get
the feeling it's coming.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.380
This flick, like a fine wine, will only get
better with age.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:53.560
Nightbreed

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:58.080
Advertised as a traditional slasher film,
Nightbreed confused critics by giving the

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:02.060
audience a dark horror fantasy that feels
more like a great young adult novel.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:06.260
That's not to say it skimps on the scares,
it just happens to also contain the worldbuilding

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.360
and character arcs you'd find in blockbuster
franchises these days.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:13.960
The story focuses on the human world clashing
with an underground city, the home of the

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.180
undead creatures known as the Nightbreed.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:24.500
"And that means you're meat for the beast."

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.939
The film came out about 20 years too early,
and it found itself in the hands of critics

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.840
who weren't quite sure what to make of it.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.600
While it sits with a terrible rating on Rotten
Tomatoes, Nightbreed is still very much worth

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:36.120
your time.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.760
It's fun, innovative, and totally singular.

